# Project-basic release-readiness record

## Scope

This is the closeout readiness record for the accepted experimental `project-basic@0.1.0`
implementation. It binds the accepted risk-review outputs into a final successor record. It does
not create or claim a Production v1 release candidate, a release, a Git tag, publication, or owner
acceptance.

## Readiness assessment

| Area | Status | Basis |
|---|---|---|
| Scoped implementation | Ready | `project-basic@0.1.0` is a declarative bundled pack with seven fixed phases, eleven read-only templates, four profiles, interview groups, and per-phase guidance. |
| Governance preservation | Ready | Standard actor, transition, claim/check/evidence/verification/owner-acceptance semantics remain unchanged; no core lifecycle or protocol change was made. |
| Existing-pack preservation | Ready | Exact `software-basic@0.6.0` and `research-basic@0.4.0` identities remain pinned and validation passed. |
| Distribution discovery | Ready within scoped evidence | The built 1.0.0 wheel installed and validated all three bundled packs on CPython 3.14 Windows venv smoke. |
| Documentation and routing | Ready | Companion, workflow selection, templates boundary, dogfood guide, README/index/user-guide routing, and historical-candidate boundary are recorded. |
| Qualitative workflow fit | Not proven | Owner-observed dogfood is intentionally planned rather than fabricated. |
| Full-suite validation | Not claimed | Focused suite passed; broad local test attempts lacked a final terminal summary. |
| Public release readiness | Out of scope | No candidate replacement, release, tag, publication, or framework version bump is authorized by this initiative. |
| Clean-worktree closure checkpoint | Ready after scoped commit | The Git/closure guide requires the reviewed branch and governed records to be committed before separately authorized terminal archival; an owner may push without waiting for CI, which remains independent evidence. |

## Residual constraints carried forward

1. Observe the five documented dogfood scenarios before claiming the project companion or guidance
   improves experience over ordinary chat.
2. Re-run the full suite in a stable terminal or CI before any broader release decision.
3. Treat dedicated CLI guidance rendering, automatic templates, conditional workflow branching, or
   persisted conversational approval as separate successor proposals, not implied follow-up work.
4. Commit the scoped branch and confirm clean `git status --short` before terminal closure; pushing
   without waiting for CI is allowed only by owner direction and does not imply a release.

## Closeout recommendation

The accepted scope is ready to close as an experimental bundled-pack implementation once this
record and lessons are verified and owner-accepted. Closing records the initiative history only;
it does not publish code or elevate the historical local candidate into current-source evidence.
